# Reading Shortcut Stories

Prefer the `shortcut` MCP server, configured at user scope against
`https://mcp.shortcut.com/mcp`. Its tools cover reading and updating stories,
and they keep the credential out of the transcript.

When the MCP server is not available on the box, the API token is at
`~/.config/shortcut/token` (mode 600):

```bash
curl -s -H "Shortcut-Token: $(cat ~/.config/shortcut/token)" \
  https://api.app.shortcut.com/api/v3/stories/193474
```

Read the token through the file every time. Never copy its value into a
worktree, a commit, a PR body, a design document, or a chat message -- expand
it inside the command, as above.

Neither route exists on every machine. If both are absent, ask for the story
contents rather than guessing them from the branch name or the diff.
